DATA. The code licence above does not cover the data, the figures or the
outputs.

The values made for this article are released under CC BY 4.0. These are the
values transcribed from published tables and figures in data/transcribed and
data/read_from_figures, each with its source in data/REGISTRY.md, the output
of their check in data/check_transcriptions_result.txt, the outputs of the
simulations in sim_out, and the images in figures.

The values derived from the open datasets keep the terms of their source.

data/open_extracted/p2_per_typist.csv and p4_per_typist.csv, their copies in
analysis/ and the outputs in analysis/ computed from the same dataset derive
from Feit AM, Weir D, Oulasvirta A, "How we type: Movement strategies and
performance in everyday typing", Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.4047775, released
under CC BY-NC 4.0. They are shared here under CC BY-NC 4.0.

data/open_extracted/throwing_per_session.csv and throwing_per_throw.csv, their
copies in analysis/ and the outputs in analysis/ computed from the same dataset
derive from Ozkaya G et al., "Three-dimensional motion capture data during
repetitive overarm throwing practice", figshare,
doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.c.4017808, released under CC BY 4.0. They are shared
here under CC BY 4.0.

data/open_extracted/karate_per_athlete.csv and karate_per_recording.csv, their
copies in analysis/ and the outputs in analysis/ computed from the same dataset
derive from Szczęsna A, Błaszczyszyn M, Pawlyta M, "Optical motion capture
dataset of selected techniques in beginner and advanced Kyokushin karate
athletes", figshare, doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.c.4981073, released under
CC BY 4.0. They are shared here under CC BY 4.0.

data/open_extracted/p5_mean_curve.csv and its copy in analysis/ hold 30 mean
scores derived from the records of Stafford T, Dewar M, axongame,
github.com/tomstafford/axongame, whose repository states no licence for the
data. They are given so that the analysis can be checked, and the records
themselves are not redistributed.

No raw file of these datasets is copied here. data/REGISTRY.md and
data/checksums give where to obtain each file and its SHA-256.
